{"type":"message","id":"f468c32f","parentId":"0c493762","timestamp":"2026-05-27T07:51:07.997Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Goal Step List:\nMove the lint pipeline's Phase 2 ref extraction (in `crates/skillet/src/lint/pipeline.rs`) and the `unused_fragment` rule (in `crates/skillet/src/lint/rules/unused_fragment.rs`) to use the new parser (`crate::compiler::parse::PanParse` and `crate::compiler::PanSource`) instead of regexes.\n\nSpecifically:\n1. In `ParsedRefs::extract` (in `crates/skillet/src/refs.rs`), replace the regex-based extraction of typed refs and untyped backticks with the new parser. Parse the source using `PanSource::new` + `PanParse::new` + `parse()`, then convert `Node::Ref` to `TypedRef`, `Node::RefSuspect` to `UntypedRef` (after classification), and `Node::Fragment` can be used by the fragment rule. Keep markdown link extraction via regex since the parser doesn't handle markdown links.\n\n2. In `unused_fragment.rs`, replace the `FRAGMENT_INCLUDE_RE` regex with the parser to detect fragment inclusions.\n\n3. All existing tests must continue to pass. The lint behavior should remain identical.\n\nNote the RefKind mapping:\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Reference` → `refs::RefKind::Ref`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Path` → `refs::RefKind::Ref` (path refs are the same as ref:: for lint purposes)\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Skill` → `refs::RefKind::Skill`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Cmd` → `refs::RefKind::Cmd`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Var` → `refs::RefKind::Var`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Env` → `refs::RefKind::Env`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Agent` and `compiler::parse::RefKind::Url` — skip for now (not used by lint rules)\n\nFor `RefSuspect`, extract the text from source using the source_range (strip the outer backticks) and pass through `classify_untyped` to get the `UntypedRef`.\n\nFor fragment detection in `unused_fragment.rs`, parse each source file and collect `Node::Fragment` values.\n\nProduce a Goal Execution Plan with:\n- An ordered Goal Step Sequence\n- Stable step ids (step-01, step-02, …)\n- A functional story for each step\n- Functional acceptance criteria per step (observable outcomes, no implementation details)"}],"timestamp":1779868267996}}
{"type":"message","id":"7a76580f","parentId":"f468c32f","timestamp":"2026-05-27T07:51:30.636Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating functional acceptance**\n\nI think functional acceptance shouldn’t get too detailed about mappings. It seems typed references of supported kinds are recognized like before, and markdown links are still acknowledged, but unsupported parser reference kinds should be ignored. Then, there's another step for the fragment rule and a final step regarding regression. I need to remember that the plan should dictate an authoritative execution order, so I’ll call emit_goal_execution_plan once to proceed.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Evaluating functional acceptance**\\n\\nI think functional acceptance shouldn’t get too detailed about mappings. It seems typed references of supported kinds are recognized like before, and markdown links are still acknowledged, but unsupported parser reference kinds should be ignored. Then, there's another step for the fragment rule and a final step regarding regression. I need to remember that the plan should dictate an authoritative execution order, so I’ll call emit_goal_execution_plan once to proceed.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_r0zGEkbP8MbiyBR1b9FN2qS5|","name":"emit_goal_execution_plan","arguments":{"steps":[{"id":"step-01","story":"Update lint reference extraction so supported references are recognized from the new parser while preserving the current lint-visible behavior.","functionalAcceptance":["When lint processes source text, supported typed references are detected through the new parser and appear to lint consumers with the same kinds and values expected today.","Untyped backtick references that should still be linted are detected from parsed source and classified into the same lint-visible categories as before.","Markdown links continue to be detected for linting exactly as they are today.","Parser node kinds that are not currently used by lint do not create new lint references or change existing lint outcomes."]},{"id":"step-02","story":"Update fragment-usage detection so the unused-fragment rule identifies fragment inclusions from parsed source instead of regex matching.","functionalAcceptance":["Fragment inclusions present in source files are recognized through the new parser for the purposes of the unused-fragment rule.","Fragments that are actually included are not reported as unused.","Fragments that are not included continue to be reported as unused with the same user-visible rule behavior as before."]},{"id":"step-03","story":"Confirm the lint pipeline remains behaviorally stable after the parser-based extraction changes.","functionalAcceptance":["All existing tests pass after the change.","User-visible lint behavior remains unchanged for the covered cases, including reference extraction and unused-fragment reporting.","No new lint findings are introduced solely because of unsupported parser node kinds that are intentionally out of scope."]}]}}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":4570,"output":541,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":5111,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779868268124,"responseId":""}}
